WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.755
Book Three, Proposition Twenty-Five.

2
00:00:02.755 --> 00:00:08.332
Given a segment of a circle, to describe the complete circle of which it is a segment.

3
00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:11.121
Let A B C be the given segment of a circle.

4
00:00:11.121 --> 00:00:16.050
It is required to construct the complete circle of which A B C is a segment.

5
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:26.746
Bisect the chord A C at D by One Ten, draw D B from D at right angles to A C by One Eleven, and join A B by Postulate One.

6
00:00:26.746 --> 00:00:33.147
Angle A B D is then either greater than, equal to, or less than angle B A D.

7
00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:35.168
First let it be greater.

8
00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:48.560
On B A at point A, construct angle B A E equal to angle A B D by One Twenty-Three; extend D B to meet A E at E by Postulate Two, and join E C by Postulate One.

9
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:55.449
Because angle A B E equals angle B A E, in triangle A B E the sides E B and E A are equal by One Six.

10
00:00:55.449 --> 00:01:06.081
Next compare triangles A D E and C D E: A D equals D C, D E is common, and the right angles A D E and C D E are equal; so by One Four the bases A E and C E are equal.

11
00:01:06.081 --> 00:01:11.590
Since A E equals both E B and E C, the three segments E A, E B, and E C are all equal.

12
00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:30.100
By Three Nine, point E—from which three equal segments fall on the arc—is the center of the circle; and constructing circle E A, with center E and defining radius point A, completes the circle whether the segment is less than, equal to, or greater than a semicircle, as was required to do.

13
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:48.395
Euclid's trichotomy of angle A B D versus angle B A D simultaneously locates the center E and classifies the given arc: E falls outside the segment when it is less than a semicircle, coincides with midpoint D when it is a semicircle, and falls inside on D B when it is greater than a semicircle.

14
00:01:48.395 --> 00:02:03.845
As Heath notes, while later editors found E by intersecting the perpendicular bisectors of two chords, Euclid's proof explicitly establishes E A equal to E B and E C so that Three Nine guarantees the constructed circle coincides with the entire given arc.

15
00:02:03.845 --> 00:02:11.480
